# The looper and FREEZE. REC records VOX from the keys (the clock starting if it is not); REC again: it
# plays, its length the nearest beat; REC while it plays: a layer over it, REC again: kept. PLAY held:
# the last layer undone; PLAY: stopped, again: from the start; REC with PLAY: cleared. FREEZE (ARP):
# the notes held keep sounding when let go; again: they let go. Audio in looper.wav.
autoplay 0
wait 300
wav looper.wav
tap REC
wait 100
expect looper 1
expect playing 1
key w2 down
wait 1000
key w2 up
wait 500
key w4 down
wait 500
key w4 up
wait 600
tap REC
wait 100
expect looper 2
expect layers 1
expect looplen 16
expect vox_notes >1
wait 8000
expect vox_notes >5
shot loop_playing.png
tap REC
wait 100
expect looper 3
tapkey w6
wait 2000
tap REC
wait 100
expect layers 2
press PLAY
wait 800
release PLAY
wait 100
expect layers 1
expect looper 2
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect looper 4
wait 12000
expect vox 0
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect looper 2
press REC
press PLAY
wait 100
release REC
release PLAY
wait 100
expect looper 0
key w0 down
key w4 down
wait 300
tap ARP
wait 100
expect frozen 2
key w0 up
key w4 up
wait 3000
expect vox 1
shot frozen.png
tap ARP
wait 100
expect frozen 0
wait 12000
expect vox 0
tap SEQ
wait 3000
wavstop
expect clips 0
